## Repro code

```js
import { ESLint } from "eslint";

const eslint = new ESLint({
    overrideConfigFile: true,
    stats: true,
    overrideConfig: [
        {
            files: ["**/*.txt"],
            processor: {
                preprocess() {
                    return [];
                },
                postprocess() {
                    return [];
                }
            }
        }
    ]
});

const [result] = await eslint.lintText("plain text", {
    filePath: "empty.txt"
});

console.log(JSON.stringify(result.stats, null, 2));
```


### What did you expect to happen?

Every entry in `stats.times.passes` should satisfy [ESLint's documented
`TimePass`](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/extend/stats) shape. 

```json
{
  "parse": {
    "total": 0
  },
  "fix": {
    "total": 0
  },
  "total": 0.293166
}
```

And in types file:

https://github.com/eslint/eslint/blob/87e0a082438264ad90b87fd74165ab4fd90f63ef/lib/types/index.d.ts#L1125-L1146


### What actually happened?


```json
{
  "times": {
    "passes": [
      {
        "fix": {
          "total": 0
        },
        "total": 0.286208
      }
    ]
  },
  "fixPasses": 0
}
```

